description: Guardrails for OCR and LLM-based card detail extraction
globs: lib/**/*.dart
alwaysApply: false
---

# Card Scan and Extraction Guardrails

- Require explicit user consent before camera capture or uploading any image for OCR/LLM extraction.
- Show a clear disclosure: what data is extracted, where processing happens, and how long data is retained.
- Treat captured images as sensitive; keep them local by default and delete immediately after extraction.
- If cloud inference is enabled, send only the minimum cropped regions required for extraction.

# Prompt and Payload Safety

- Never include full user profile, unrelated app data, or stored card records in OCR/LLM prompts.
- Minimize payload fields to card text extraction only (holder name, PAN, expiry, network hint).
- Mask PAN in UI previews and logs; do not render full PAN from model output until user confirms.
- Block extraction flows from auto-saving data without user review.

# Quality and Fallback Behavior

- Use confidence thresholds per field; low-confidence fields must require manual correction.
- Provide a manual entry/edit screen as first-class fallback for OCR/LLM failures.
- Validate extracted values with deterministic checks before persistence.
- Keep an audit-friendly local event trail without sensitive payload content.

# Agent Refusal Behavior

- Refuse implementations that silently upload raw camera images without consent.
- Refuse any request that persists source card photos long term without explicit user opt-in and retention controls.
